lice use radar or  laser based detectors to spot speeders  they can also follow a car called pacing  to confirm it's going too fast  captain Grenon says it's about targeting  enforcement to try to prevent deadly  crashes we're looking at where these  accidents occurred how can we change  people's behaviors in terms of speeding  and driving more safely I think the  biggest way to do that is just by being  present out there Virginia does not  currently allow speed cameras and we  should tell you deaths on the roads have  soared over the last two years an  estimated 14 percent to around 40,000  and the NTSB says an unintended  consequences of states that have raised  speed limits has been more deaths gale  all right thank you Chris
 

